#!/usr/bin/env python3
# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
"""
nr-nostr -- the Nostr twin of nr-announcer: posts every paid jukebox request as a Nostr note from the Jukebox
Lightning Bot identity, as it goes on air. Nostr is free, so the note carries the station link. Stdlib only:
BIP-340 Schnorr signing, NIP-19 bech32 and a small WebSocket client live in this file. No new software on the ship.

HOW IT WORKS
  Every 10 s it reads the station's own public /api/nowplaying. A track with requested=true and a new req_id is
  a paid request going on air. One note per request, sent to every relay in the list; one relay saying OK is a post.
  The words come from the SAME rules as the X announcer (this program imports /usr/local/bin/nr-announcer for
  clean(), the blocklist and the message rules), plus a second line with the station link. When the station hands
  over the Wavlake artist's npub, the note mentions the artist (nostr:npub...) and tags them, so they see it.
  Every note that carried a message, and every withheld message, is shown to SF in Telegram (admin-notes channel).

KEYS
  /home/sf/.config/nr-nostr/nostr.env holds NOSTR_NSEC=... (600, owner sf), written by nr-nostr-keys.py through a
  masked prompt. The key never appears in a log, a journal line, --check output or chat. --check prints the npub.

SWITCHES (files in /home/sf/.config/nr-nostr, no restart needed)
  LIVE      exists -> posts for real.   Absent -> DRY: logs "[dry] would post: ..." and nothing leaves the box.
  OFF       exists -> idles.            relays.txt  EVERY relay to send to, one per line (the installer writes the four
            public ones; a line in this file REPLACES the built-in list, so keep them when adding your own).
  The blocklist is the announcer's: /home/sf/.config/nr-announcer/blocklist.txt.

LIMITS
  MAX_PER_HOUR (default 20). A note no relay accepts is retried next cycle, three times, then given up with one
  Telegram line. Relay trouble reaches SF ONCE per 6 h.

RUN  (systemd: nr-nostr.service, User=sf)      nr-nostr
     nr-nostr --check      config status (prints the npub, never the key)      nr-nostr --once   one poll cycle
     nr-nostr --selftest   offline: BIP-340 vectors, bech32, event id, WebSocket framing against a fake relay
"""
